{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\n// Defined in trust_but_verify.\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports an execution error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.execute`. I did not request any implementation source. This is based on the supplied test text only.\n\nThe requirement has three obligations:\n1. `execute` receives a context for the criterion's source node.\n2. An `Ok` value is the completed answer.\n3. An `Err` value is an execution error, using the variants `Graph`, `NoAgentConfigured`, `Agent` and `Output`. The future must also be `Send`.\n\n**Context for the source node, and the `Ok` answer**\n- `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` runs `verify(Review(Node(1)))`. It asserts the completed output (`result` false, `rationale` \"ordinary computation\") and a `Dependency::Node(Node(1), …)` fingerprint, so the context reads the source node.\n- `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` checks the returned answer (`output().get() == 17`). It requires the futures to be `Send`, using the `send` helper, and checks that answers are stored and reloaded.\n- `criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs` shows that a negative `false` answer is an `Ok`. It checks the answer, its `Node(1, \"false\")` dependency, and the stored output `json!(false)`.\n- `review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` shows that a negative determination is a completed answer. The answer is returned unchanged and contains `determination` and `rationale`. It is persisted and reloaded with non-empty dependencies, and `Review.source_node_id()` is the node.\n\n**`Err` execution errors**\n- **`Graph`:** `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs` makes a callback read fail. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"missing\"))` and that nothing is stored.\n- **`NoAgentConfigured`:** `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` asserts `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)`. It also asserts no records and no reads. After an agent is attached, the same criterion succeeds.\n- **`Agent`:** `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error` asserts `ValidationError::Agent(_)` both from `ctx.ask` and from `verify`. It also asserts no record is stored. `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` checks that the `Agent` payload is a `String` and checks its display and `source` behaviour.\n- **`Output`:** `criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer` feeds non-JSON content. It asserts `ValidationError::Output(e)` with `e.is_syntax()` and an empty store.\n\nEvery named variant and the success path have a test that exercises it and asserts the outcome. The tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unmarked relevant test and no unacknowledged gap.",
